# File Naming Rules

## All Files Must Use Kebab-Case

- **All files** (components, utilities, pages, API routes, etc.) must be named in **kebab-case** (lowercase letters with hyphens).
- This applies to:
  - Component files (`.tsx`, `.ts`, `.jsx`, `.js`)
  - Utility files
  - Page files
  - API route files
  - Configuration files (when applicable)
  - Any other source files

## Examples

✅ **Correct:**
- `auth-provider.tsx`
- `form-field-text.tsx`
- `platform-delete-dialog.tsx`
- `user-profile.tsx`
- `api-handler.ts`

❌ **Incorrect:**
- `AuthProvider.tsx` (PascalCase)
- `FormFieldText.tsx` (PascalCase)
- `platformDeleteDialog.tsx` (camelCase)
- `user_profile.tsx` (snake_case)
- `APIHandler.ts` (PascalCase)

## Component Files

- Component files under `components/` must use kebab-case.
- The component name itself (exported function/class) can still be PascalCase, but the file name must be kebab-case.
- Example: File `auth-provider.tsx` exports `export function AuthProvider() { ... }`

## When Creating New Files

- Always use kebab-case when creating new files.
- If you see a file that's not in kebab-case, rename it to kebab-case and update all imports.
